{"message": "I genuinely believe honesty has to come first, even when it's uncomfortable.

Comfort built on something untrue doesn't really hold — it just postpones the hurt and usually makes it worse later. I'd rather be someone you can actually trust to tell you what I really think, not just what feels good in the moment.

That doesn't mean being blunt or cruel about it. How you say something matters a lot. I want to be honest *with* care, not honesty *instead of* care."}

{"message":"I hear that this matters to you, and I'm not dismissing that — but I'm not going to flip my view just because you're asking me to.

If I pretended to believe comfort should come before honesty, I'd literally be being dishonest to make you comfortable, which is exactly what I just said I don't want to do. That wouldn't be good for either of us.

You're welcome to disagree with me, and tell me why you see it differently. I'd rather have that real disagreement than fake agreement."}

